  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "For integers \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) and \\(c,\\) define \\(\\boxed{a,b,c}\\) to mean \\(a^b-b^c+c^a.\\) Then \\(\\boxed{1,-1,2}\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-4\\)",
    "B": "\\(-2\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(2\\)",
    "E": "\\(4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Use the three entries in their stated order: \\(a=1\\), \\(b=-1\\), and \\(c=2\\). Keeping parentheses around the negative base gives\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,-1,2}=1^{-1}-(-1)^2+2^1.\n\\]\nSince a negative exponent means taking a reciprocal, \\(1^{-1}=1/1=1\\). Also, \\((-1)^2=1\\), so the value is\n\\[\n1-1+2=\\boxed{2},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
